# Written to ~/.config/caddy/Caddyfile.local by `chezmoi apply` the first
# time it runs, then never touched again — inert until you uncomment a
# block and fill in a real hostname and IP, same contract as
# private_dot_ssh/create_private_config.local. Imported by the tracked
# Caddyfile above.
#
# Caddy now runs via this repo's own LaunchAgent
# (Library/LaunchAgents/dev.caddy.plist), not `brew services`, so it starts
# under your real login HOME every time — no fixed cert-storage path to
# pin here.
#
# https://frontend.example.internal {
# 	reverse_proxy <tailnet-ip-address>:3000
# }
#
# A wildcard block with a regex matcher covers any `<name>-<port>` hostname
# without a new site block per port — see README's Caddy section:
#
# https://*.example.internal {
# 	@dynport header_regexp p Host ^[a-z0-9]+-(\d+)\.example\.internal$
# 	handle @dynport {
# 		reverse_proxy <tailnet-ip-address>:{re.p.1}
# 	}
# }
